Description: Keep software ISP unity-gain threshold in real gain units
 CameraSensorHelper::gain takes a register code. Passing 1 interpreted a code
 of 1 as unity (1/128 for OV13B10), so an overexposed scene could remain stuck
 at minimum gain and never reduce exposure. Use the real unity/lower bound.
Author: TB710FU local adaptation
Forwarded: no
--- a/src/ipa/simple/soft_simple.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/soft_simple.cpp
@@ -227,7 +227,7 @@
 	if (camHelper_) {
 		context_.configuration.agc.againMin = camHelper_->gain(againMin);
 		context_.configuration.agc.againMax = camHelper_->gain(againMax);
-		context_.configuration.agc.again10 = camHelper_->gain(1.0);
+		context_.configuration.agc.again10 = std::max(1.0, context_.configuration.agc.againMin);
 		context_.configuration.agc.againMinStep =
 			(context_.configuration.agc.againMax -
 			 context_.configuration.agc.againMin) /
